# Naming Conventions

## Purpose

Improve readability, clarify intent, reduce bugs, enforce predictability, enhance maintainability, and support clean code practices.

## General Rules

- Variables and functions: **camelCase** — `isRegistered`, `userList`
- Booleans must read like questions: `isVisible`, `hasAccess`, `canSubmit`
- No vague names: `data`, `info`, `temp` are banned

## File and Folder Naming

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Folders | `kebab-case` | `class-search`, `home-page`, `alerts` |
| React Components | `PascalCase` | `ClassSearch.tsx`, `HomePage.tsx` |
| Utility / Hook files | `camelCase` | `useData.ts`, `fetchHelper.ts` |
| Constants / Enums | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `API_ENDPOINTS.ts`, `ENV_KEYS.ts` |

## Variable Naming

### Booleans

| Prefix | Intent | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `is` | State or identity | `isLoading`, `isActive` |
| `has` | Ownership or presence | `hasAccess`, `hasErrors` |
| `can` | Ability or permission | `canEdit`, `canSubmit` |
| `should` | Recommendation or decision | `shouldRender`, `shouldRetry` |
| `show` / `hide` | User interaction–driven visibility | `showModal`, `hideModal` |

### Arrays / Lists

| Format | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Plural noun | Preferred | `users`, `products`, `classes` |
| `xList` | Explicit list reference | `userList`, `courseList` |
| `xArray` | Type disambiguation | `errorArray`, `idArray` |

### Numeric / Count

| Format | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Count / Total | Total items | `totalUsers`, `courseCount` |
| Index | Position or loop | `index`, `currentIndex` |
| Limit | Min / max threshold | `maxAttempts`, `minScore` |

### Objects

| Format | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Entity object | Single model | `user`, `settings`, `formData` |
| Grouped values | Related config fields | `studentDetails`, `accountInfo` |
| API response | Data from backend | `response`, `apiResponse`, `classScheduleData` |

### Strings

| Format | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Plain string | UI text or messages | `pageTitle`, `errorMessage`, `labelText` |
| Identifier | Unique / reference value | `userId`, `sessionToken`, `classCode` |
| Status / type key | Enum or type indicator | `userRole`, `statusCode`, `paymentType` |
| Formatted output | Logic or format result | `formattedDate`, `displayName` |

## Git Commit Format

Pattern: `<type>: <storyId> <description>`

Example: `fix: 223981 corrected button logic`

- No special characters other than the colon separator.
- Always include the user story ID for traceability.

| Type | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New feature for the user |
| `fix` | Bug fix for the user |
| `refactor` | Restructures code without changing behavior |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `style` | Formatting, whitespace, missing semicolons — no logic change |
| `test` | Adding or correcting tests — no production code change |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `build` | Build tools, CI pipeline, dependencies, project version |
| `ops` | Infrastructure, deployment, backup, recovery |
| `chore` | Miscellaneous (e.g., `.gitignore` updates) |
